Translation patch: `PreviousGtidsEvent`/`PreviousGtidsSid`: loops and tags

Change: The nested `for` loops of `deserialize` become the recursive helpers `parse_sids`/`parse_sid`/`parse_intervals`; `io::Error::new(kind, "..")` becomes `io_error_msg`; `into_owned`'s `into_iter().map(..).collect()` becomes the recursive `sids_into_owned` (using `Vec::pop`); `is_tagged`'s `iter().any(..)` an index loop; the `serialize` loops index loops. The operations on `packets::Tag` (validation via `str::from_utf8` + `Tag::new` with their `format!` errors, `Tag::into_owned`, `tag.as_str().as_bytes()`) move into opaque helpers in `binlog::trusted` (`previous_gtids_tag`, `tag_into_owned`, `tag_as_bytes`).
Why: Early returns (`?`) in loops, closures, `Vec` `into_iter` and `iter().any` are not supported by Aeneas; `Tag` validation iterates `str::chars`, and `Cow<str>` ownership goes through `ToOwned for str`, neither modelled.
Behaviour: Identical: the helpers run the same iterations in the same order with the same early exits; `sids_into_owned` converts the elements in order (popping recurses to the front first); the trusted helpers are the moved expressions.

